From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:21:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: nt36536: OnePlus Pad 4: stock's front porch for
 144 Hz

The 144 Hz mode had a horizontal front porch of 68. Stock's table for this
panel gives 32 / 16 / 20 (front porch / sync / back porch) per DSI link at
144 Hz, which is 64 / 32 / 40 for the whole panel; 68 is the sum of the
three per-link numbers. All other modes already are twice stock's
per-link values.

Use 64: the line is 3528 instead of 3532 pixel clocks long and the pixel
clock 1259.9 instead of 1261.3 MHz.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c
index 8d0ac3bc6397..0d9b7ec4e228 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c
@@ -629,11 +629,11 @@ static int csot_iceland_init_seq(struct mipi_dsi_multi_context *dsi_ctx,
 static const struct drm_display_mode csot_iceland_modes[] = {
 	{
 		/* 144Hz */
-		.clock = (3392 + 68 + 32 + 40) * (2400 + 26 + 2 + 52) * 144 / 1000,
+		.clock = (3392 + 64 + 32 + 40) * (2400 + 26 + 2 + 52) * 144 / 1000,
 		.hdisplay = 3392,
-		.hsync_start = 3392 + 68,
-		.hsync_end = 3392 + 68 + 32,
-		.htotal = 3392 + 68 + 32 + 40,
+		.hsync_start = 3392 + 64,
+		.hsync_end = 3392 + 64 + 32,
+		.htotal = 3392 + 64 + 32 + 40,
 		.vdisplay = 2400,
 		.vsync_start = 2400 + 26,
 		.vsync_end = 2400 + 26 + 2,
-- 
2.43.0

